---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DemoGallery from '../../components/DemoGallery.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Website demos" current="demos" description="Explore RevaCSS website demos, Living Blueprint and the experimental Effects Lab. Customize their appearance and download HTML starters." documentation>
  <p class="doc-kicker">REVACSS / DEMOS</p>
  <h1>See what you can build.</h1>
  <p class="doc-lead">Complete websites and original experiments built with RevaCSS components. Explore their pages, change the shared appearance settings and download HTML for your own project.</p>
  <DemoGallery/>
  <p class="doc-note"><a href={base+'demos/hero/'}>Try heroes with animated gradient text and translucent background light</a>. Includes subtle, expressive, glass and static examples with a native pause control.</p>
  <p class="doc-note">Native CSS source preview: <a href={base+'demos/reading-progress/'}>try the reading-progress bar</a> on a full-length page. This optional decoration is separate from the website starters; browser acceptance is pending.</p>
  <section class="doc-section"><h2>Make a demo your starting point</h2><ol><li>Open a demo and use <strong>Customize</strong> to choose its colours, material, spacing and navbar.</li><li>Download the HTML from the customizer. Without JavaScript, copy the chosen attributes into the supplied source.</li><li>Download its linked CSS assets and update paths for your own hosting.</li><li>Replace the fictional content and connect forms or commerce features to your application.</li></ol><p>The CSS core and native component interactions work without browser JavaScript. The optional documentation helper saves appearance choices and prepares customized downloads.</p><a class="button outline" href={base+'guide/'}>Get started with RevaCSS</a></section>
</Layout>
